course: dictionary
lesson: 14479
title: Pasture: grass, animals and new beginnings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pasture is a field of grass where cows, sheep or horses eat. «The farmer's cows grazed in the pasture all summer.» The words cows, grazed and summer are the clues: they tell you the pasture is a grassy field where animals eat.
explain: Pasture can also be a verb, a doing word. «Each spring, Mr Patel pastures his horses in the far field.» Here pasture means putting animals in a field so they can eat the grass. Ask yourself: is it a place, or something someone does?
explain: Sometimes pasture is used in a picture sense. «Our class is moving on to pastures new next year.» Moving on and new are the clues. It means starting somewhere new, which might be better. Try your meaning in the sentence to check: «Our class is moving on to a field of grass next year» does not make sense, so the picture meaning is right.
fact: A pasture is grassland where animals graze.
fact: Pasture can be a noun (the place) or a verb (to put animals there to eat grass).
fact: «Green pastures» can mean a peaceful, happy place.
fact: In Psalm 23 from the Bible, «He maketh me to lie down in green pastures» is a picture of God caring for people like a shepherd.
fact: «Put out to pasture» means someone has retired from work.
exercise: «The cows grazed all afternoon in the green pasture.» What is a pasture? | A farm building | A type of fence | A kind of cow | *A field of grass where animals eat
exercise: «Each morning, the farmer pastures the sheep on the hill.» What does pastures mean here? | To clean the barn | To build a fence | *To put animals in a field to eat grass | To sell animals at market
exercise: «We are moving on to pastures new next year.» What does this mean? | A holiday by the sea | A field full of grass | A school trip to a farm | *A new place or start that might be better
test: «The horses rested in the pasture after their long run.» In this sentence, what kind of word is pasture? | An adjective, a describing word | *A noun, a place | A verb meaning to run fast | A verb, a doing word
test: In Psalm 23, «green pastures» is a picture of what? | *Peace and care | A big storm | Hard work on a farm | Losing a game
exam: «The old teacher was put out to pasture after forty years.» What does put out to pasture mean? | Moved to a new school | Sent out to play | *Retired from work | Fed on fresh grass
